{
  "manufacturer": "Yaskawa",
  "manufacturer_slug": "yaskawa",
  "model": "F7 drive (CIMR-F7U, legacy) - Modbus RTU",
  "model_slug": "f7",
  "short_model": "F7",
  "aliases": [
    "CIMR-F7U",
    "F7U",
    "F7 Drive"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
  "applies_to": "Yaskawa F7 (CIMR-F7U) general-purpose drives using the built-in RS-422/485 terminals R+/R-/S+/S-, per user manual TM.F7.01 Appendix D, with parameter and monitor addresses from TM.F7.11.",
  "summary": "The F7 is Yaskawa's legacy general-purpose vector drive with an embedded Modbus RTU slave on terminals R+/R-/S+/S-. Commands are written to hex registers 0001H-000FH, detailed fault/alarm words sit at 0010H-001AH, status and PID levels at 0020H-003FH, and each parameter has a hex address. This map covers the full Appendix D reference and monitor data plus fault codes and the b1/H5 setup parameters.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 31,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "hex 0-based",
    "note": "Register numbers are hex and go on the wire unchanged: the 03H message example reads starting address 00 20 (drive status). Parameter addresses are the hex values in the TM.F7.11 parameter tables (b1-01 = 0180h, H5-01 = 0425h)."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "F7 Drive User Manual (Appendix D Communications)",
    "doc_number": "TM.F7.01",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.yaskawa.com/delegate/getAttachment?documentId=TM.F7.01&cmd=documents&documentName=TM.F7.01.pdf",
    "pages": "Appendix D: function examples pp. D-7 to D-9, reference data p. D-10, monitor data pp. D-11 to D-15, broadcast/enter p. D-16"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Parameter addresses (b1, H5) and U2/U3 monitor addresses come from the free F7 Drive Parameter Access Technical Manual TM.F7.11 (2005-11-30): https://www.yaskawa.com/delegate/getAttachment?documentId=TM.F7.11&cmd=documents&documentName=TM.F7.11.pdf (Table 4.4 monitor registers, Tables 4.6 and 4.11 parameters).",
    "Left out because neither manual gives units or resolution for them: 0025H-0028H and 0031H, and the 0040H-006CH U1 monitor block.",
    "b1-01/b1-02 also accept codes beyond 3 (pulse input, CASE reference); only the common 0-3 selections are listed.",
    "Fault code numbers for U2/U3 registers are not tabulated, so no value list is given.",
    "The Modbus TCP/IP DPRAM table in TM.F7.11 (registers 2000h-2010h) applies only to the Ethernet option card and is not included.",
    "Broadcast (slave 0): 0001H bit 0 run, bit 1 reverse, bits 5/6 inputs S3/S4, bits C-F S5-S8 (enabled by 000FH bits C-F); 0002H = 30000 per 100 % of max frequency."
  ],
