        "address": 128,
        "why": "Current fault code"
      },
      {
        "table": "holding_register",
        "address": 25,
        "why": "Alarm content 1"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "H5-01 address (default 1Fh, 0-20h), H5-02 baud (default 3 = 9600), H5-03 parity (default none); cycle power. b1-01 = 2 and b1-02 = 2 select serial communication for reference and run.",
    "watchdog": "H5-05 = 1 (default) enables communication fault (CE) detection; H5-04 selects the reaction: 0 ramp, 1 coast, 2 fast-stop, 3 alarm only (default). 002CH bit F shows a comm time-out. No detection-time parameter is listed for the F7.",
    "quirks": [
      "Registers and addresses are hex and 0-based.",
      "Function codes 03H, 06H, 08H and 10H.",
      "Parameters written over Modbus need an Enter command: 0 to 0900H (EEPROM, 100,000 writes max) or 0910H (RAM only).",
      "Write 0 to unused bits and never write reserved registers."
    ],
    "setup": [
      "Terminals S+, S-, R+, R-; for RS-485 jumper S+ to R+ and S- to R-. Up to 31 drives.",
      "8 data bits, 1 stop bit; 1200-19200 baud; parity none/even/odd.",
      "Power-cycle after changing H5-01..H5-03."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Fault trace data is not recorded for CPF00, CPF01, CPF03, UV1 and UV2."
    ]
